{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And the ra'ah, etc., לְמִינָהּ.</b> It appears that every species among the twenty-four (Ḥullin 63a) that has many varieties and divergent forms, Scripture states concerning it לְמִינֵהוּ or לְמִינֵיהֶם, whereas every species that has only a few varieties that are somewhat similar, Scripture does not state לְמִינוֹ. And the proof is that concerning the nesher (vulture/eagle) לְמִינוֹ is not stated, yet the Gemara says (Ḥullin 61a) regarding a certain bird that is not recognizably a nesher that they are concerned it may be a species of nesher — see, the nesher does have varieties, and even so Scripture did not state לְמִינוֹ."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:17:22.689959407Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}